romdev-pycparser

A plain JavaScript port of pycparser 2.23 as vendored, with GCC-extension
patches, by m2c (m2c_pycparser, m2c commit
1d1c4454a445326541305f83f2b0cb680a9ecb2d) and by decomp-permuter
(perm_pycparser, decomp-permuter commit
41bd0bfc32aa5ea78de4cf28be603163256c2a4c). The two vendored copies are the
same files under two package names.

pycparser is Copyright (c) 2008-2022, Eli Bendersky. PLY (Python Lex-Yacc)
is Copyright (C) 2001-2017, David M. Beazley (Dabeaz LLC). Both are
BSD-licensed; the full license texts are in LICENSE.

src/tables/lextab.json, src/tables/yacctab.json and src/tables/c_ast.json are
data converted from the upstream lextab.py, yacctab.py and c_ast.py by
scripts/gen-tables.mjs (which reads them as Python literals; nothing runs
Python). The lexer and LALR parse loop follow PLY 3.10's ply/lex.py and
ply/yacc.py; the grammar actions, AST, generator and AST transforms follow the
upstream c_parser.py, plyparser.py, c_ast.py, c_generator.py and
ast_transforms.py.

The test suite under test/ is a port of the upstream pycparser tests; the C
files under test/fixtures/c_files are copied from upstream's tests/c_files.
